# ============================================================
#  Generic social events — `actor: any`.
#  The engine binds `npc` to one met character for whom `when`
#  is true. Use rel(npc), love(npc), bond(npc), romanceable(npc),
#  tagged(npc, faculty) in conditions and {npc}, {they}, {them},
#  {their}, {They} in text. These drive the relationship system:
#  friendships form, romances spark, rivalries flare, bonds decay.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Friendship ----------------

@event soc_study_session
title: Study Session
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where (tagged(npc, student) or tagged(npc, prefect)) and rel(npc) >= 0
per: npc
trigger: social
when: term and not wrapup
repeat: 4
art: book
tags: social study
scene: Two students at a candlelit table piled with books, one explaining something with wild hand gestures.
text: {~{npc} drops into the seat across from you with an armful of books. "Exams are coming for us all. Misery loves company. Study with me?"|{npc} slides a stack of notes onto your table. "I've read this chapter four times and it's still in a foreign language. Help?"|{npc} finds you in the library and sits down without asking. "If I study alone I'll just reorganise my quills. Keep me honest?"}
> left: You work better alone
  lore +tiny
  rel npc -tiny
  say: You get a lot done. {~{npc} sits at the next table and sighs loudly every few minutes.|{npc} finds someone else, and their laughter carries across the library all evening.|{npc} leaves you a biscuit on the way out, which somehow makes it worse.}
> right: Pull up a chair
  mood -tiny
  lore +small
  study +tiny
  rel npc +small
  say: You get half as much done and remember twice as much of it. {~{npc} explains the Third Law with a biscuit diagram.|You quiz each other until the candle gutters.|{npc} makes up a rude rhyme for every date, and you will never forget a single one.}

@event soc_borrow_money
title: A Small Loan
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and rel(npc) >= 3
per: npc
trigger: social
when: gold >= 20
repeat: 6
art: pouch
tags: social money
scene: A student holding out an empty purse upside down with a sheepish grin.
text: {npc} turns out an empty purse. "I'm fifteen crowns short {~for rent|for the term's ink and parchment|for the wand-mender, and it's my only wand}. I'll pay you back. I swear on my wand."
> left: Sorry, you're tight too
  rel npc -small
  say: "No, of course, I understand." {They} {are} quiet at dinner.
> right: Lend fifteen crowns
  gold -medium
  alignment +tiny
  rel npc +medium
  chance likely:
    queue soc_loan_repaid in 2 with npc
    say: {npc} hugs you with the empty purse still in {their} hand.
  else:
    say: {npc} hugs you. You suspect you will never see those fifteen crowns again.

@event soc_loan_repaid
title: Paid Back
class: story
tone: light
trigger: queued
actor: npc
art: coin
tags: social money
scene: A small stack of coins and a sweet bun left on a desk with a thank-you note.
text: {~{npc} finds you after class and presses a little stack of coins into your hand, plus a sticky bun. "Fifteen crowns. And interest." The interest is the bun.|{npc} turns up at breakfast with a small purse and a very straight face. "Fifteen crowns. I said I would."|{npc} slides fifteen crowns across the library table, one coin at a time. The last one has a note under it: "Thank you. Really."}
> left: Count it
  gold +medium
  rel npc +small
  mood +tiny
  say: You count it, because {they}'d be offended if you didn't. Fifteen exactly. {npc} nods, satisfied, as if a debt of honour has been settled.
> right: Pocket it without counting
  gold +medium
  rel npc +small
  mood +tiny
  say: You put it away uncounted. {npc} looks quietly pleased to be trusted, which was worth more than the crowns.

@event soc_become_friends
ramp: rel(npc) 18..30
title: Something Like Friendship
class: milestone
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and bond(npc) == "none" and rel(npc) >= 18
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 20
art: group
tags: social
scene: Two students walking across the lawn at sunset, laughing at the same joke, shadows long behind them.
text: {npc} saves you a seat without asking now, and you save {them} one. You trade notes, complaints and the last biscuit without keeping score. Somewhere along the way, this became a friendship.
> left: Keep a little distance
  rel npc +tiny
  say: You stay friendly. Just not too close. Some walls are load-bearing.
> right: Call it what it is
  bond npc friend
  rel npc +medium
  mood +small
  say: "So we're friends now," {npc} says. "Officially." You shake on it, solemnly, then ruin it by laughing.

@event soc_become_close
ramp: rel(npc) 36..50
slot: night
title: The Kind of Friend You Call at 3am
class: milestone
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and bond(npc) == "friend" and rel(npc) >= 36
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 18
art: heart
tags: social
scene: Two friends sitting on a dormitory floor at 3am wrapped in one blanket, empty mugs between them.
text: It's 3am. You can't sleep, and you've walked to {npc}'s door before you've even decided to. {They} open{s} it before you knock.
> left: Apologise and go back to bed
  rel npc +small
  say: "Don't be daft," {npc} says, but lets you go. In the morning there's tea outside your door.
> right: Talk until sunrise
  bond npc close
  rel npc +medium
  mood +medium
  say: You tell {them} things you haven't told anyone. {They} tell you things back. The sun comes up and neither of you notices.

@event soc_secret
title: A Secret
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and rel(npc) >= 15
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: lock
tags: social
scene: Two students huddled under a staircase, one whispering into the other's ear, a finger to their lips.
text: {~{npc} pulls you under the stairs. "I need to tell someone or I'll burst. Swear you won't tell anyone. Not even the portraits."|{npc} closes the dormitory door, checks it, and checks it again. "I have to tell someone. Swear you'll keep it."|{npc} walks you to the far end of the lake path, where nobody goes. "Can you keep something? Really keep it?"}
> left: "I'd rather not carry it."
  rel npc -tiny
  say: {npc} looks hurt, then relieved. "Maybe that's better." You'll never know.
> right: "I swear."
  mood -tiny
  rel npc +medium
  guile +tiny
  say: {~It's not a big secret. It's the kind that's only big to the person holding it. You hold it with {them}.|It's about a letter from home, and it's heavier than {they} let on. You carry half of it now.|It's ridiculous, and {they} know it's ridiculous, and {they} needed someone else to know anyway. You do.}

@event soc_argument
title: Words Exchanged
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and rel(npc) >= 6 and bond(npc) != "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 6
weight: 8
art: bolt
tags: social
scene: Two students facing off in an empty corridor, one with arms crossed, the other mid-gesture, both flushed.
text: It starts with something small — {~a borrowed book, a joke that landed wrong|whose turn it was to fetch the tea|a seat someone saved and someone else took} — and suddenly you and {npc} are arguing {~in the corridor|on the stairs|in the middle of the refectory}, louder than either of you intended.
> left: Apologise first
  rel npc +small
  mood -tiny
  say: {~"I'm sorry." {npc} deflates. "...Me too." It's over. It feels better than winning would have.|You say sorry first. {npc} looks almost disappointed not to get to say it. You share a bun about it later.|"I'm sorry." {npc} blinks, then laughs. "We were both being absurd." You were.}
> right: Stand your ground
  mood -tiny
  chance even:
    rel npc -medium
    say: {npc} storms off. You were right. It doesn't feel as good as you'd hoped.
  else:
    rel npc +medium
    charm +small
    say: You argue it out until you're both laughing at how ridiculous it got. Somehow you're closer after.

@event soc_village_trip
title: A Day in the Village
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and rel(npc) >= 6
per: npc
trigger: social
when: gold >= 5
repeat: 5
art: house
tags: social
scene: A cobbled village street with crooked shopfronts, two students sharing a paper cone of roasted nuts.
text: "Barge to the village? Tea at Mabel's, a wander round the bookshops, back before curfew?" {npc} is already wearing {their} coat.
> left: Not this week
  rel npc -tiny
  say: {~{They} bring{s} you back a cinnamon bun anyway.|{They} bring{s} you back a postcard of the village, which is three streets long.|{They} come{s} back with a story about a goat and tell{s} it badly.}
> right: Grab your coat
  gold -tiny
  mood +medium
  rel npc +small
  say: {~Tea, buns, a bookshop cat that sits on {npc}'s feet. You almost miss the last barge, laughing.|Mabel's, then the market, then a long argument about which bun is best. You get the last barge home with sticky fingers.|Rain, so you spend the whole afternoon in the bookshop. {npc} buys a book about knots and explains every one on the barge home.}

@event soc_friend_sick
title: Sick Friend
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and (bond(npc) == "friend" or bond(npc) == "close" or bond(npc) == "partner")
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: rain
tags: social
scene: A student tucked into an infirmary bed under a mountain of blankets, a friend sitting beside them with a bowl of soup.
text: {npc} has Lake Fever and is miserable in the infirmary. Sister Amaranth says visitors are allowed, but she won't be responsible.
> left: Send a card
  rel npc +tiny
  say: You send a card with a drawing of Sister Amaranth as a dragon. {npc} keeps it on {their} bedside table.
> right: Sit with them every evening
  rel npc +medium
  alignment +tiny
  chance unlikely:
    gain sick
    say: You keep {them} company for a week. Then you're in the next bed. You both find this hilarious.
  else:
    say: {~You read aloud, badly, doing voices. {npc} recovers and claims it was the voices.|You teach {them} every card game you know and lose all of them. {npc} recovers, insufferably.|You bring soup from the kitchens every evening and tell {them} all the gossip. {npc} recovers mostly out of curiosity.}

@event soc_gift_given
title: A Small Gift
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and rel(npc) >= 9
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 7
art: gem
tags: social
scene: A small wrapped parcel tied with ribbon left on a dormitory pillow, a pressed flower tucked into the bow.
text: There's a small parcel on your pillow. A note in {npc}'s handwriting: "Saw this and thought of you. Don't make it weird."
> left: Thank {them} later
  mood +tiny
  rel npc +tiny
  say: {~It's a tiny brass compass that always points to the nearest teapot. You use it constantly.|It's a bookmark that hums when you stop reading. Annoying. You love it.|It's a pair of gloves that stay warm all winter. You wear them until they're threadbare.}
> right: Get {them} something back (8 gold)
  gold -small
  mood +small
  rel npc +medium
  say: You find {them} {~a book {they}'d wanted for months|a scarf in exactly {their} colour|a sketchbook with good paper}. {npc}'s face when {they} open{s} it is worth twice the price.

@event soc_drift
title: Drifting Apart
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and rel(npc) >= 6 and rel(npc) < 24 and apart(npc) >= 2
per: npc
trigger: social
when: since(soc_drift) > 3
weight: 6
repeat: 6
art: hourglass
tags: social
scene: A student glancing back across a busy courtyard at another who hasn't seen them, the space between them full of strangers.
text: You realise you haven't really talked to {npc} in weeks. You see {them} {~across the courtyard|at the far end of the refectory|on the library steps}, laughing with people you don't know.
> left: Let it be
  rel npc -small
  say: People drift. It's nobody's fault. You still smile when you pass in the halls.
> right: Go over and say hello
  chance likely:
    rel npc +medium
    mood +tiny
    say: {~"There you are!" {npc} says, as if you'd been the one missing. Maybe you had.|{npc} introduces you to everyone as "the one I told you about". You wonder what {they} told them. It seems to have been good.|{npc} shifts over to make room on the bench without a word, as if your seat had been waiting.}
  else:
    rel npc +tiny
    mood -tiny
    say: You go over. It is friendly, and short, and you both say "we should catch up" in a way that means you won't.

@event soc_rumour
title: Rumours About {npc}
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 9 and not tagged(npc, villager)
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: paper
tags: social
scene: A cluster of students whispering behind their hands in a corridor, glancing toward someone just out of view.
text: A nasty rumour about {npc} is going round {~the common room|the refectory|the library steps}: {~that {they} cheated on an exam|that {they} {are} leaving at the end of term in disgrace|that {they} said something cruel about a friend}. It's not true. You know it's not true. People are laughing.
> left: Let it blow over
  mood -tiny
  say: It blows over. {npc} never finds out you heard it. You find out you don't like yourself for it, a little.
> right: Shut it down
  alignment +tiny
  challenge negotiate apprentice:
    win:
      rel npc +medium
      renown +small
      say: You make the rumour-monger look so foolish that the story dies on the spot. {npc} hears about it later and just squeezes your arm.
    lose:
      rel npc +small
      renown -tiny
      say: You make a scene and now there are rumours about you too. {npc} thinks you're an idiot. A loyal idiot.

@event soc_homework_help
title: Desperate Homework
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where (tagged(npc, student) or tagged(npc, prefect)) and rel(npc) >= 0
per: npc
trigger: social
when: term and not wrapup
repeat: 5
art: feather
tags: social study
scene: A student with ink on their face clutching a half-finished essay, another student leaning over to read it.
text: {npc} waves a half-finished {~essay|lab report|star chart} at you. "It's due in an hour and I've written the title twice. Help."
> left: Explain the concept
  challenge research apprentice:
    win:
      rel npc +medium
      lore +tiny
      say: You explain it so clearly that {npc} finishes the essay with time to spare. {They} insist{s} you're a genius.
    lose:
      rel npc +tiny
      say: You explain it so confusingly that you both end up more lost. You hand it in together, two confused people against the world.
> right: "Copy mine."
  alignment -tiny
  rel npc +small
  chance unlikely:
    study -small
    rel npc -tiny
    say: The professor notices two identical pieces of work. You both get detention, a lecture, and a note on your record that every one of your professors reads.
    gain detention
  else:
    say: {npc} hands it in and gets a better mark than you did. Unbelievable.

@event soc_faculty_advice
title: A Word of Advice
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, teacher) and rel(npc) >= 6
per: npc
trigger: social
when: term and not wrapup
repeat: 6
art: scroll
tags: study
scene: A professor walking with a student along a covered walkway, pointing at something in an open book.
text: {npc} catches you after a lecture. "You've been working hard. Or hardly working. I can never tell with your year. Some advice, if you'll take it?"
> left: Politely decline
  rel npc -tiny
  say: "Suit yourself." {They} walk{s} off. Faculty have long memories.
> right: Listen carefully
  mood -tiny
  rel npc +small
  study +small
  lore +tiny
  say: It's good advice about how to study, {~annoyingly good|delivered at great length|illustrated with a story from {their} own disastrous first year}. Every piece of work you hand in that month is better for it.

# ---------------- Romance ----------------

@event soc_spark
title: A Spark
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where romanceable(npc) and rel(npc) >= 9 and spark(npc) < 12 and bond(npc) != "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
when: bonds(partner) == 0
weight: 12
repeat: 6
art: sparkle
tags: social romance
scene: Two hands brushing as they reach for the same quill, both students freezing for a heartbeat.
text: You and {npc} reach for {&the same quill|the last biscuit on the plate|the same library book} at the same moment. Your hands touch. Neither of you lets go immediately. {&It's a perfectly ordinary quill.|It's a perfectly ordinary biscuit.|It's a perfectly ordinary book.}
> left: Laugh it off
  rel npc +tiny
  say: "All yours," you say. {npc} laughs. The moment passes. Mostly.
> right: Hold on a moment longer
  chance likely:
    spark npc +medium
    rel npc +tiny
    say: {npc} looks up. Something in {their} face shifts. Then {they} let{s} go, a little pink, and {&the quill rolls under the desk|the biscuit breaks neatly in half|the book falls open on the floor between you}.
  else:
    rel npc +tiny
    mood -tiny
    say: {npc} pulls back as if burned, and the rest of the {&lesson|meal|afternoon} is very, very awkward.

@event soc_date
title: An Invitation
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where romanceable(npc) and spark(npc) >= 12 and spark(npc) < 40 and bond(npc) != "partner" and rel(npc) >= 9
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 12
repeat: 4
art: heart
tags: social romance
scene: A student nervously holding out a hand-drawn ticket to the village's floating lantern show.
text: You could ask {npc} to {&the lantern show in the village|the travelling players at the Newt|the music on the quay} this weekend. As friends. Or, you know. Not as friends.
> left: Ask as friends
  gold -tiny
  rel npc +small
  mood +small
  say: You pay for both tickets and the hot cider. It's a lovely evening. You're both very careful about elbows.
> right: Ask as more than friends
  if spark(npc) >= 25:
    challenge negotiate apprentice likely wild:
      win:
        spark npc +medium
        mood +medium
        say: {npc} says yes before you finish the sentence. You hold hands through the whole {&show and miss every lantern|play and miss every line|evening and miss every song}.
      lose:
        spark npc -tiny
        mood -small
        say: {npc} hesitates, then says {they}'d rather go as friends. It's a nice evening. It's a long evening.
  else:
    challenge negotiate apprentice wild:
      win:
        spark npc +medium
        mood +medium
        say: {npc} says yes before you finish the sentence. You hold hands through the whole {&show and miss every lantern|play and miss every line|evening and miss every song}.
      lose:
        spark npc -tiny
        mood -small
        say: {npc} hesitates, then says {they}'d rather go as friends. It's a nice evening. It's a long evening.

@event soc_confess_generic
ramp: spark(npc) 30..45
title: Feelings, Spoken
class: milestone
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where romanceable(npc) and spark(npc) >= 30 and rel(npc) >= 18 and bond(npc) != "partner" and bond(npc) != "ex"
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 10
art: heart
tags: romance
scene: Two students standing very close on a windswept bridge between towers, one with a hand over their heart.
text: On the bridge between the towers, the wind snatching at your robes, you realise you can't keep it in anymore. {npc} is looking at you like {they} know what you're about to say.
> left: Say nothing
  spark npc -small
  say: The moment passes. You walk back together, a careful inch apart.
> right: Tell {them}
  challenge negotiate apprentice likely +1 if spark(npc) >= 60:
    win:
      bond npc partner
      spark npc +medium
      mood +large
      say: "Finally," {npc} says, and kisses you, and the wind steals your breath anyway.
    lose:
      spark npc -large
      mood -medium
      say: {npc} takes a long breath. "I care about you," {they} say{s}. "Just not like that. I'm sorry." The wind is very cold.

@event soc_partner_date
title: Date Night
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 3
weight: 14
art: candle
tags: romance
scene: Two people at a tiny candlelit table in a window alcove of a village tea shop, snow falling outside.
text: {npc} has booked the window table at Mabel's. Candles. {season == "winter": Snow outside.|The lake going gold outside.} "We're splitting the bill," {they} say{s}. "Don't argue."
> left: Talk about the future
  gold -tiny
  spark npc +small
  mood +small
  say: {&You talk about where you'll be in ten years. In every version, you're both there.|You talk about after graduation, carefully, then not carefully at all.|You make a list of places you'll go together. It is already too long.}
> right: Talk about absolutely nothing
  spark npc +tiny
  mood +medium
  say: You argue for an hour about {&whether soup is a drink|whether owls are smart or just look it|which professor would win in a duel}, and {npc} pays the bill while you're making your closing argument. {&It is the best date of your life.|It might be better than the last one.|You lose the argument and don't mind.}

@event soc_partner_neglect
title: "You're Always Busy"
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "partner" and apart(npc) >= 3
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 14
repeat: 5
art: hourglass
tags: romance
scene: A person waiting alone at a table set for two, a candle burned low, the other chair empty.
text: {npc} is waiting outside your door. "I feel like I only see you in corridors," {they} say{s}. "Do you even want this?"
> left: "I'm sorry. I'll make time."
  spark npc +tiny
  mood -tiny
  study -tiny
  say: You skip a study session for a long walk by the lake. It's the right call.
> right: "You know how busy I am."
  spark npc -medium
  rel npc -medium
  say: {npc} nods slowly. Something between you cools a degree.

@event soc_breakup
title: The End of Something
class: routine
tone: grim
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "partner" and spark(npc) < 25
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 30
art: heartbreak
tags: romance crisis
scene: Two people sitting on opposite ends of a bench in a grey garden, not looking at each other, rain beginning.
text: {npc} sits down at the far end of the bench. "I think we both know," {they} say{s} quietly. "This isn't working anymore."
> left: Fight for it
  challenge negotiate journeyman:
    win:
      spark npc +large
      say: You talk for hours. It's raw and honest and it hurts. And at the end, {npc} takes your hand again.
    lose:
      bond npc ex
      gain heartbroken
      rel npc -large
      say: You try. It only makes it harder. In the end you're both crying, and it's over anyway.
> right: Let {them} go
  bond npc ex
  gain heartbroken
  rel npc +small
  say: You agree. It's terrible and gentle and right. {npc} kisses your forehead once before {they} leave{s}.

@event soc_two_timing
title: Found Out
class: incident
tone: grim
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
when: bonds(partner) >= 2
weight: 40
art: heartbreak
tags: romance crisis
scene: A person holding up two crumpled love letters in a crowded corridor, the crowd parting around them.
text: {npc} is holding two letters. One is to {them}. The other isn't. "I found it in your bag," {they} say{s}, very quietly. Half the corridor has stopped to watch.
> left: Beg forgiveness
  challenge negotiate journeyman- unlikely:
    win:
      spark npc -large
      rel npc -large
      say: {npc} doesn't forgive you. But {they} don't leave. Not yet. You're on borrowed time.
    lose:
      bond npc ex
      rel npc -huge
      renown -medium
      gain heartbroken
      say: {npc} tears both letters in half and walks away. Everyone knows by dinner.
> right: Say nothing
  bond npc ex
  rel npc -huge
  renown -medium
  say: Your silence is an answer. {npc} drops the letters at your feet and leaves. The story is all over the academy.

@event soc_ex_encounter
title: Awkward
class: milestone
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "ex"
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 6
art: mirror
tags: romance
scene: Two people coming face to face in a narrow library aisle, both holding books, neither moving.
text: {~You turn into the library aisle and there's {npc}. Your ex. Holding the same book you came for.|The only free seat in the refectory is opposite {npc}. Your ex. {They} look{s} up at the same moment you do.|You open the door to the owlery and there's {npc}. Your ex. Holding a letter, halfway to an owl.} Neither of you moves.
> left: Turn around and leave
  mood -tiny
  say: You find a different book in a different aisle and read the same paragraph six times.
> right: Say hello like a person
  rel npc +medium
  challenge negotiate apprentice-:
    win:
      bond npc friend
      say: It's awkward for one minute, then it isn't. You end up laughing about the worst of the dates you went on. Friends, maybe. Really.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: "Hello." "Hello." You both stand there. Then you both leave. It's a start.

# ---------------- Rivalry ----------------

@event soc_rival_taunt
title: A Public Taunt
class: routine
tone: tense
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and (bond(npc) == "rival" or bond(npc) == "nemesis" or rel(npc) <= -12)
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 4
art: mask
tags: rival
scene: A smirking student surrounded by a small audience, pointing at someone across a crowded dining hall.
text: In the middle of a crowded {~meal|common room|library queue}, {npc} loudly recounts {~your most embarrassing moment of the term|the time you walked into a door that was a painting|your worst spell in front of the whole class}. People laugh. {They} look{s} very pleased.
> left: Ignore {them}
  mood -small
  say: The laughter dies down. {~You carry on with as much dignity as you can find.|You wait it out, and stare at a fixed point on the wall.|Someone nearby passes you a biscuit in silent solidarity.}
> right: Fire back
  challenge negotiate vs npc.charm:
    win:
      renown +small
      rel npc -small
      say: {~Your comeback is so good that someone at the far table applauds.|Your comeback lands so well that people repeat it for a week.|Your comeback is quiet, exact and devastating.} {npc} goes scarlet.
    lose:
      renown -small
      rel npc -tiny
      say: Your comeback comes out as a squeak. The laughter doubles.

@event soc_make_peace
ramp: rel(npc) 3..15
time: noon afternoon
title: Burying the Hatchet
class: milestone
tone: tense
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and (bond(npc) == "rival" or bond(npc) == "nemesis") and rel(npc) >= 3
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 18
art: hand
tags: rival social
scene: Two former rivals shaking hands on a dueling green at sunset, wands tucked away.
text: {npc} finds you after class, scuffing {their} shoes. "This whole rivalry thing. It's getting tiring. Truce?"
> left: Keep the edge
  rel npc -small
  say: "Thought so," {npc} says, half-smiling. The game goes on.
> right: Shake on it
  bond npc friend
  rel npc +large
  mood +small
  say: You shake. It's strange — you know {them} better than most of your friends. Maybe that's the point.

@event soc_rival_bet
title: The Wager
class: routine
tone: tense
cast:
  npc: any where (tagged(npc, student) or tagged(npc, prefect)) and bond(npc) == "rival"
per: npc
trigger: social
when: term and not wrapup
repeat: 6
art: dice
tags: rival
scene: Two students slapping coins onto a table between them, a crowd gathering, a chalked tally on the wall.
text: "Eight crowns says I {~outscore you in the next practical|light more candles in one breath than you|hold a ward longer than you}," {npc} says, slapping coins on the table. A crowd forms.
> left: Decline the bet
  rel npc -tiny
  say: "Thought so." {npc} pockets the coins. You decide not to care. You care.
> right: Take the bet
  when: gold >= 8
  challenge spell vs npc.arcana wild:
    win:
      gold +small
      renown +small
      rel npc +small
      say: You win by a hair. {npc} pays up with a theatrical bow. "Next time."
    lose:
      gold -small
      rel npc +tiny
      say: You lose by a hair. "Next time," you say. {npc} grins. "Next time."

# Spark crossing @balance spark_follow's cooldown mark (playtest 2, M37): the engine asks once whether you want it.
@event spark_cooldown
title: Something Between You
trigger: queued
actor: npc
defer: off_campus or not around(npc)
class: milestone
tone: warm
art: rose
tags: romance social
scene: Two students on a bench a little closer than friends usually sit, both pretending to read the same page.
text: Something has shifted between you and {npc}. {~They hold your gaze a moment too long.|They've started saving you a seat, and blushing about it.|Your names keep turning up next to each other in other people's gossip.} You could let it grow, or gently let it cool.
> left: Let it grow
  say: {~You don't say anything. You don't move away either.|You hold their gaze back, for exactly as long.|Let them gossip. You sit beside them anyway, in front of everyone.}
> right: Let it cool, kindly
  cool npc
  rel npc +tiny
  say: {~You find a gentle way to say you value them as a friend. They look relieved, or almost.|You keep it light and friendly, and the moment passes. The friendship stays.|You give the gossip nothing to work with, gently, and in a week it moves on. The friendship doesn't.}

# ---------------- Jealousy (playtest 2, N7; design §8.2): two people with a spark for you, neither your partner yet ----------------

@event jealousy_two_invitations
title: Two Invitations
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
cast:
  suitor: any where romanceable(suitor) and spark(suitor) >= 30 and bond(suitor) != "partner" and around(suitor)
  other: any where romanceable(other) and spark(other) >= 30 and bond(other) != "partner" and around(other)
per: suitor
repeat: 2
weight: 20
art: heart
tags: romance social
scene: A student holding two folded notes, one in each hand, in a corridor where two people wait at opposite ends.
text: Two notes in one morning. {suitor} asks if you're free on Friday evening, in neat handwriting, crossed out once. {other} asks the same, for the same evening, in a hurry. They both know the other asked. The whole corridor seems to know.
> left: Say yes to {suitor}
  spark suitor +small
  spark other -small
  rel other -tiny
  say: Friday with {suitor} is everything the note promised. On Saturday {other} passes you on the stairs with a smile that stops a little short of the eyes.
> right: Say yes to {other}
  spark other +small
  spark suitor -small
  rel suitor -tiny
  say: Friday with {other} runs late and warm. On Saturday {suitor} is very polite to you at breakfast, which is worse than if they'd been rude.

@event jealousy_seen_together
title: "Who Was That?"
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
cast:
  suitor: any where romanceable(suitor) and spark(suitor) >= 30 and bond(suitor) != "partner" and around(suitor)
  other: any where romanceable(other) and spark(other) >= 30 and bond(other) != "partner" and around(other)
per: suitor
repeat: 2
weight: 20
art: heartbreak
tags: romance social
scene: Two students talking by a window in a crowded common room, one of them asking a question too casually while looking at someone across the room.
text: {suitor} saw you laughing with {other} in the courtyard yesterday, and is now asking about it too casually, in the voice people use when they've rehearsed. "You two looked… close. Not that it's any of my business."
> left: Tell the truth: you like {other}
  spark suitor -small
  rel suitor +tiny
  spark other +tiny
  say: It lands like a dropped plate. {suitor} nods, and swallows, and thanks you for not pretending. It's the kindest thing you've done all week, and it doesn't feel kind at all.
> right: "Oh, we're just friends"
  chance likely:
    spark suitor +small
    say: {suitor}'s shoulders come down an inch. You spend the rest of the evening together, and nobody mentions the courtyard again.
  else:
    spark suitor +tiny
    spark other -small
    say: It goes well, until word gets back to {other}, who hears "just friends" and decides to believe it.

@event jealousy_cold_supper
title: A Quiet Supper
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
cast:
  suitor: any where romanceable(suitor) and spark(suitor) >= 30 and bond(suitor) != "partner" and around(suitor)
  other: any where romanceable(other) and spark(other) >= 30 and bond(other) != "partner" and around(other)
per: suitor
repeat: 2
weight: 20
art: meal
tags: romance social
scene: A long refectory table at supper, one student eating in pointed silence beside another, a third person waving from the far end of the hall.
text: {suitor} has gone quiet at supper, and answers in single words. From the far end of the hall, {other} is waving you over to an empty seat. You know exactly why {suitor} is quiet. So, by the look of it, does {other}.
> left: Stay and talk it through
  spark suitor +small
  spark other -tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: A long walk after supper and a careful, clumsy conversation. {suitor} laughs at the end of it, which is something. At the far end of the hall, the empty seat stays empty.
> right: Take the seat {other} saved
  spark other +small
  spark suitor -small
  say: The seat is warm and so is {other}. Behind you, {suitor} finishes supper alone and leaves without the pudding, which everyone notices.
